# The MetaRocq bytestring bridge, kept out of the rocq-base64 package so that
# depending on it does not pull in MetaRocq; it is installed on its own, as
# rocq-base64-bytestring (`make bytestring`).  That build does not use this file
# -- it compiles against the installed library, not `../theories` -- this is
# here so editors resolve the two logical paths.
-Q . Base64.MetaRocq
-Q ../theories Base64

Bytestring.v
Tests.v
